{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793742863,"nonce":"fhl7tkc2pzipc6gifp+ftN3tSSg=","title":"Provision isolated anonymous landing-demo sessions","message":"Add an explicit public-demo admission flow in the Rust Worker and runner. The current loopback --preview-project bootstrap is intentionally local and must not be exposed publicly or embedded with a fixed token. Admit only the operator-pinned Pocket Studio release for anonymous visitors, mint short-lived scoped lease/session capabilities, and keep the runner credential and GitHub tokens private. The editor must appear before admission and show connecting/ready/error state while the remote session is attached.\n\nUse independent workspace/state volumes and document identity per visitor; no shared live Git tree or CRDT authority. Bound launches and retries, rate-limit admission, keep an aggregate concurrency cap, and expire abandoned leases with cleanup. Reconnect only to the same lease/generation; fence expired/reassigned sessions. Resolve initial browser edits into the new session through the CRDT flow without overwriting them. Signing in may offer an explicit import/save into an owned workspace; do not treat anonymous ownership as a GitHub account identity.\n\nDone when two clean browsers edit and run independent demo sessions, cannot read each other, reload/reconnect retains only the right live state, and failed/full admission keeps the editor usable with loading/retry feedback. Verify real built-in extension processes and no fixed local-port/origin assumptions.\n\nPart of landing deployment: git-bug 56b531e22a0bf22913529f321d5b0f7d3ab02bef3d18192d73838675fff95704","files":null}]}